# chad-webui-mcp — MCP stdio server that exposes chad-webui sub-commands
# as native MCP tools.
#
# Why this exists: openclaw can register MCP servers via
# `openclaw mcp set <name> <json>`. Once registered, the gateway loads
# them on startup and the agent sees each tool with its JSON schema in
# the system prompt. The model can then call (e.g.) the
# `calendar_create_event` tool with structured args, and the
# gateway routes the call here. We translate the call into a
# `chad-webui calendar create-event --flag …` subprocess invocation and
# return the JSON stdout.
#
# This gives Chad the same fail-closed per-operator scoping as direct
# CLI use (chad-webui reads CHAD_OPERATOR_SLUG from env) but with
# structured tool-call audit instead of opaque exec lines.
#
# Protocol: MCP version 2024-11-05, JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio.
# Stdlib-only; no external deps. The server reads one JSON-RPC message
# per line on stdin, writes one response per line to stdout.

